re, but the wording "either equal to one month\'s rent or more" suggests that both possibilities exist. So, the deposit could be exactly $2000 or higher, but it can\'t be less than that.\n\nTherefore, the statement in the question is accurate because it correctly captures that the deposit is either exactly $2000 or more. There\'s no information that contradicts this, so the statement is true.\n</think>.\nThe security deposit at the Olive Garden is never less than one month\'s rent ($2000), contradicting the given information.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
