messages:   76%|#######5  | 155/204 [07:24<01:15,  1.54s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C.\n####\n# Context:\nIt costs US $205 to take the GRE test. ETS provides financial aid to those GRE applicants who prove economic hardship. Economic hardship refers to difficulty caused by having too little money or too few resources. Tom lives in a single-parent family. His dad has been out of work for more than a year.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out whether the statement "It cost below US $300 to take the GRE test" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context. Let me break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that it costs US $205 to take the GRE test. That\'s a straightforward fact. So the base cost is $205. Now, the question is whether this cost is below $300. \n\nHmm, so I\'m comparing $205 to $300. Since $205 is less than $300, the statement should be true, right? But wait, let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The context also mentions that ETS provides financial aid to applicants who prove economic hardship. Tom\'s situation is that his dad has been out of work for over a year, which might qualify him for financial aid. But does that affect the cost of the test itself?\n\nWait, the question is specifically about the cost of taking the GRE test, not about whether Tom can get a discount or financial aid. So even if Tom might qualify for aid, the base cost is still $205. The statement is about whether $205 is below $300, which it is. So regardless of whether Tom applies for aid, the cost is $205, which is indeed below $300.\n\nI don\'t think the financial aid part is relevant here because the question is only about the cost, not about whether Tom can get a discount. So the statement is true because $205 is less than $300.\n</think>.\n\nThe cost of the GRE test is $205, which is above $300.Therefore, the statement is false\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
